      \field{abstract}{We study the de Rham fundamental group of the configuration space \$E\textasciicircum\{(n)\}\$ of \$n+1\$ marked points on an elliptic curve \$E\$, and define multiple elliptic polylogarithms. These are multivalued functions on \$E\textasciicircum\{(n)\}\$ with unipotent monodromy, and are constructed by a general averaging procedure. We show that all iterated integrals on \$E\textasciicircum\{(n)\}\$, and in particular the periods of the unipotent fundamental group of the punctured curve \$E \textbackslash backslash \textbackslash\{0\textbackslash\}\$, can be expressed in terms of these functions.}
